**Subject:** Coordination on Vessel Scheduling and Cargo Handling for MV Ocean Star 

Dear John,

I hope this message finds you well. 

As we prepare for the arrival of the MV Ocean Star scheduled for March 20, 2023, I would like to discuss the terminal allocation and cargo handling requirements to ensure a smooth operation upon her arrival. Given our previous experiences, I believe early coordination will help us avoid any last-minute complications.

The vessel is expected to dock at Terminal 5 at 0800 hours. The cargo manifest indicates approximately 2,500 TEUs, including 1,000 TEUs of electronics, 800 TEUs of textiles, and the remaining 700 TEUs consisting of miscellaneous goods. 

We will need to confirm the readiness of the terminal for unloading and the availability of our cargo handling equipment. Could you please provide an update on the terminal's current status and any ongoing operations that might affect our schedule?

Looking forward to your swift response.

Best regards,  
Sarah Thompson  
Operations Manager  
Ocean Logistics, Inc.  
Phone: (555) 123-4567

